TI  - Copeland choice rules
AU  - Bhardwaj, Bhavook
AU  - Manocha, Kriti
PY  - 2026
T2  - Social Choice and Welfare
AB  - Tournaments are well studied objects in economic theory. Copeland ( 1951 ) provides an intuitive way to select alternatives from a tournament, the Copeland set . As a tournament solution, the Copeland set possesses many desirable properties and has been widely studied. Rubinstein ( 1980 ) axiomatizes a method to rank alternatives from a tournament which is based on their Copeland scores . This paper analyzes the Copeland set from a revealed preference perspective. A choice procedure where a decision maker has a fixed underlying tournament and selects the Copeland set from every menu is behaviorally characterized.
